Results are not reported for specimens containing exogenous or endogenous substances, which substantially interfere with the test. These include but are not limited to:
Exogenous compounds introduced by gel-barrier tubes other than the NMR LipoTube;
Endogenous protein levels ≥12 g/dL (normal range 6.0 to 8.3 g/dL);
Endogenous compounds that present interferences equivalent to exogenous sources listed above.
Improper specimen storage and handling may be destructive to lipoproteins and cause results to not be reported.

